      "writtenOn": "2016-11-07T12:30:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "that\u0027s about as bad as the previous version, just for different constants.\nIMO, what is really defined is that you have the following structure:\nEither\nSTART I2C_Addr Reg_index Data_Wr1 Data_wr2 STOP\nor \nSTART I2C_Addr Reg_index START/REP_START Data_Rd1 Data_RD2 STOP\n\nSo, you should reset the index after a STOP,\nand set it on the first data (after START and addr).\nActually a lot of gas gauge have auto-increment, so on STOP you might just increment the index.",
